carbon-server: the online server for the browser port of Need for Speed: Carbon.

The virtual network for the game's own Online mode (src/lan.rs, src/trace.rs) follows the
design of nfsu2-web by th0mk (github.com/th0mk/nfsu2-web, the server behind nfsu2.xyz),
read at commit 53e04ea (2026-10-24): its LAN switch (web/server-rs/crates/lan) and its
virtual host (web/server-rs/crates/online/src/vhost.rs and trace.rs). Taken from it: the
frame layout and the 8-byte LAN header, the TCP-over-frames operations (SYN, SYNACK, RST,
DATA, FIN, GONE) without sequence numbers or retransmission, virtual addresses in 10.77.0.0
with the server's own host at 10.77.0.1 and the source rewritten to the sender's address,
broadcasts to everyone but the sender, a virtual host that accepts a SYN with SYNACK, and
lan_frame() in src/lan.rs, which is adapted from vhost.rs. The rest of this crate is its own
code. nfsu2-web's licence:

